# Third-party licences

The `dmem` binary in a release archive has the Rust crates listed below compiled into it.
This file gives each crate's licence text, as those licences require.

Scope: the `dist` build (`cargo build --release --locked --features dist`) for the four
release targets (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu, aarch64-apple-darwin
and x86_64-pc-windows-msvc), without dev- and build-dependencies. A crate that only some of
those targets compile in is listed once for all of them. The file is generated by
cargo-about from `about.toml` and `about.md.hbs`; do not edit it by hand (see
`scripts/package-release.sh`).

dm-lite's own code is under the Apache License 2.0 (`LICENSE`, `NOTICE`). The native vector
library that ships beside the binary (zvec, with Apache Arrow built in) and AWS-LC are
covered in `NOTICE`, and the AWS-LC licence text is in `THIRD-PARTY-aws-lc.txt`.

